{"title":"Electricity","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Overview\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Overview</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#The_circuit\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">The circuit</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Power_Source\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Power Source</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Resistors\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Resistors</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Extra_Components\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Extra Components</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Capacitors\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Capacitors</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Transistors\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Transistors</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Sensors\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Sensors</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Overview\">Overview</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Electricity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Overview\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Electricity is the flow of electrons. It can be captured in certain liquids and solids.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"The_circuit\">The circuit</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Electricity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: The circuit\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The Circuit is currently as of July 6, 2019, the only way to harnesses electricity and put it to work. Most circuits have These components.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Power_Source\">Power Source</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Electricity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Power Source\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The power source of a circuit supplies electrons and when the electrons are finished it takes the back. Without a Power Source, it would not be powered.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Resistors\">Resistors</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Electricity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Resistors\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Resistors diffuse some of the electric and may have a proper function like a light bulb or a fan. Anything that consumes electricity and gives less back is a resistor. Always have a resistor in your circuits. It there is no resistance the current is 100%. Also, the resistor needs to be big enough.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Extra_Components\">Extra Components</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Electricity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Extra Components\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>These components allow you to do a variety of things.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Capacitors\">Capacitors</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Electricity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Capacitors\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Capacitors store <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=DC\" title=\"DC\">DC</a> energy and releases it later. Capacitors only store <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=DC\" title=\"DC\">DC</a> and let <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AC\" title=\"AC\">AC</a> pass though with a little resistance.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Transistors\">Transistors</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Electricity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Transistors\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>These direct current different ways.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Sensors\">Sensors</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Electricity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Sensors\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Sensors detect and/or measure input. \n</p>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Light_sensors&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Light sensors (page does not exist)\">light sensors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Touch_sensors&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Touch sensors (page does not exist)\">touch sensors</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Motion_sensors&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Motion sensors (page does not exist)\">motion sensors</a></li></ul>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Electricity&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Physics\" title=\"Physics\">Physics</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=Electricity&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018083331\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.018 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.034 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 38/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 274/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.344      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    6.344      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17614:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018083331 and revision id 115260. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}